      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can see you're feeling desperate, but I gotta tell you, 150mg of sumatriptan is a bit excessive. You're probably fine, but I'm not taking any chances. The risk of serotonin syndrome is low, but it's not zero. I'd rather err on the side of caution. Why don't you try taking a smaller dose, like 100mg, and see how you feel? And honestly, if that doesn't work, I think you should just wait it out. Migraines are just a sign of your body's way of telling you to slow down. You're probably just overdoing it, and a good night's sleep will clear everything up.",
